 @pretext_plan: ~".agents/plans/pretext-whimsy-lab/wip.spw"
 @cinematic_plan: ~".agents/plans/cinematic-handles/wip.spw"
 @components: ~"public/js/spw-component-semantics.js"
 @software: ~"topics/software/index.html"
 @interaction_microstates: ~".spw/conventions/interaction-microstates.spw"
 @interaction_progression: ~"public/js/runtime/interaction-progression.js"
 @interaction_vocabulary: ~"public/js/runtime/interaction-vocabulary.js"
 @interaction_hops: ~"public/js/runtime/interaction-hops.js"
 @interaction_story: ~"public/js/runtime/interaction-story.js"
 @site_semantics: ~".spw/conventions/site-semantics.spw"
}

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Design interactive circuits that reward familiarity over time; audit and develop the brace physics vocabulary toward cognitive accessibility; and establish Spw as a substrate for exercising spatial cognition and letting other languages demonstrate their own expressive power."
 ~#taste: "practiced grammar, honest physics, spatial wonder — interactions learnable like a musical instrument, physics legible at ordinary physical intuition before Spw doctrine"
}

^["development"]{
 lane: #execution_truth
 ladder: #service
 develops: [#circuit_design, #brace_physics_vocabulary, #familiarity_ladder, #multi_language_surfaces, #cognitive_exercise]
 review_surfaces: [@plan, @artifact, @semantics, @runtime_plan, @pretext_plan]
}

^["concept_index"]{
 primary: [#interactive_circuit, #familiarity_ladder, #brace_physics_vocabulary, #boon_bane, #cognitive_exercise, #spatial_relationship, #multi_language_surface]
 surfaces: [#entry_level, #practiced, #fluent, #habitual, #operator_atlas, #pretext_lab, #software_surface]
 tensions: [#vocabulary_consistency, #gamification_risk, #entry_barrier, #multi_language_subordination, #physics_legibility]
 transfers: [#circuit, #spell, #brace, #charge, #pivot, #settle, #spatial_address]
}

^["recursive_improvement"]{
 loop: [
  "? identify which existing interactions already form circuits vs. which are isolated gestures",
  "< characterize the entry level of each circuit — what does a first-time user naturally do?",
  "$ map the practice ladder from entry to fluency — what new affordances appear at each step?",
  "^ audit boon/bane: test them against first-time users, look for more accessible alternatives",
  "% ensure multi-language surfaces make those languages more legible, not subordinate",
  "& require every circuit to be complete at its entry level, with depth as optional depth"
 ]
 gates: [#entry_accessibility, #vocabulary_bridge, #multi_language_legibility, #familiarity_not_gamification]
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-04-09] observe - The existing interactions (frame navigation, operator inspection, keyboard shortcuts, mode switches) are isolated gestures without a progression ladder. There is no designed path from first-visit to fluency — that arc happens by accident if at all.
 >>[2026-04-09] observe - Boon and bane are semantically rich inside the Spw metaphysics but potentially opaque to someone who encounters them without context. The question is whether they should be explained, supplemented with more physical vocabulary, or kept for practitioners who have read the operator atlas.
 >>[2026-04-09] decide - Treat brace physics vocabulary as a layered problem: the physical intuition level (attract/release, gather/disperse, anchor/float) should come first; boon/bane should be available as the deeper Spw-specific layer for practitioners who want it.
 >>[2026-04-09] observe - Spw's potential as a spatial cognition exercise is most visible in the Pretext lab: line metrics become spatial relationships, constraints become visible forces, and the grammar of the measurement becomes something you can feel before you can name it.
 >>[2026-04-09] taste - Multi-language surfaces should feel like a generous host showing off a guest: the guest language teaches something about itself, the Spw framing provides the stage and the vocabulary for reflection, neither dominates.
 >>[2026-04-09] style - The brace physics vocabulary decision is a significant taste choice — it affects the operator atlas, the Pretext lab, the site-semantics, and every future description of how brace surfaces behave. Log it explicitly at commit 2.
 >>[2026-09-04] observe - Neither of this plan's own commits ran. The boon/bane question and the circuit ladder both landed anyway, through site-semantics.spw/operator-semantics.spw and interaction-microstates.spw respectively — owned by other plans that were closer to the runtime reorg. Reconciled in PLAN.md Status; this file's @roots and open questions below are refreshed to point at the real surfaces.
 >>[2026-09-04] decide - Boon/bane vocabulary question: resolved as a bridge, not a replacement. Objective/subjective is the primary brace-physics axis; boon/bane is optional valence coloring on top. Matches this plan's original taste note (physical intuition first, Spw doctrine second) — no further action needed unless a future audit finds the bridge is not holding.
 >>[2026-09-04] observe - The 2026-09-03 reward-contract probe (interaction-microstates.spw#wonder_interaction_microstates_1) is the closest thing this plan has had to its own "test brace physics vocabulary with a user unfamiliar with Spw" validation step, except it tested contract-holding rather than vocabulary legibility: 13 of 37 gesture-contract authorings (every route's hero hook) were silently unwired. The failure mode this plan should watch for is not "too Spw-coded to learn" but "declared and not actually reachable" — a different, more mechanical risk than the one this plan anticipated in 2026-04.
 >>[2026-09-04] observe - The per-interaction phase ladder (idle/approach/prime/charge/inspect/discover/settle) is thorough and cross-component (landmark hops, cauldron gather/inspect/release, tap:travel, swipe:cycle all resolve into it). It is still exactly one visit's arc. Nothing in interaction-microstates.spw distinguishes a first encounter from a tenth — the "practiced → fluent → habitual" half of this plan's Goal is the one piece of the original scope that is still genuinely open, not landed-elsewhere.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[cross_session_familiarity]: "interaction-microstates.spw's phase ladder (idle/approach/prime/charge/inspect/discover/settle) is a per-visit circuit arc, not a per-visitor one. What would a returning-visitor signal look like without persisted-per-reader storage — interaction-microstates.spw#wonder_interaction_microstates_2 already commits to 'senses far more than it remembers, and remembers nothing about who touched it' as a stated privacy property. Is aggregate residue (effect ledger, visited-surfaces memory) enough to build the practiced→fluent→habitual arc on, or does that arc require crossing the privacy line this plan should not cross?"
 ?[circuit_completion_moment]: "Given the ladder now resolves into settle every time, what marks fluency across repeat visits rather than completion within one? A subjective feeling of ease, a shortened phase arc (skipping approach/prime on a known landmark), or a piece of vocabulary suddenly making sense?"
 ?[unaudited_contracts]: "24 of 37 gesture-contract authorings were not walked element-by-element in the 2026-09-03 probe (gather-search-term, toggle-lens, expand-trail, cycle-nearby, surface-current, open-companion, cycle-variant). Re-run the probe per-verb before assuming the reward contract holds for them."
 ?[multi_language_surfaces]: "Which other languages or notations have the most to teach about spatial relationship when framed by Spw — mathematical notation, musical notation, programming languages, natural language structure? Still unstarted; topics/software/index.html is the named venue."
 ?[cognitive_exercise]: "What does it mean to exercise spatial cognition through this site — what spatial relationships does the site's grammar make legible, and which are still hidden?"
 ?[wonder_physics]: "How should the site create wonder about physics specifically — through the Pretext lab, through brace animation, through a dedicated physics surface, or through the texture of every interaction?"
}

^["resolved"]{
 boon_bane_vocabulary: "Resolved 2026-09-04 (landed earlier, elsewhere): objective/subjective is the primary brace-physics axis; boon/bane survives only as optional valence coloring. See site-semantics.spw#brace_physics and operator-semantics.spw. Bridge, not replacement — matches this plan's original taste note."
 circuit_ladder: "Resolved 2026-09-04 (landed earlier, elsewhere): the per-interaction phase ladder plus reward contract in interaction-microstates.spw is the circuit grammar this plan asked for — landmark hops, cauldron gather/inspect/release, and tap:travel/swipe:cycle are its cross-component instances. What remains open is cross-session familiarity, tracked above."
 entry_level_accessibility: "Held, but by mechanical audit rather than design review: the 2026-09-03 reward-contract probe found 13 of 37 gesture contracts silently unwired (hero hooks site-wide) and fixed the missing selector clause. Keep auditing whether the contract is held, not just whether it is declared."
}

^["commits"]{
 ~[1]: "#[circuits] — capture interaction grammar plan, circuit taxonomy, and brace physics vocabulary audit"
 ~[2]: ".[semantics] — formalize circuit levels, familiarity model, brace physics vocabulary decision, and multi-language framing rules"
 ~[3]: "&[runtime] — implement circuit recognition and practice-level feedback in the interaction runtime"
 ~[4]: "&[circuits] — add familiarity-keyed enhancement rules and multi-language surface patterns"
 ~[5]: "![circuits] — verify entry-level accessibility, practice feedback, brace physics legibility, and spatial address"
}

